<h2 class="mt-12">Common failure modes in deliverability email</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Failure</th><th>Prevention</th><th>Cost of getting it wrong</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Discount in the first touch</td><td>Hold offers until intent is established</td><td>Trains low-margin buying habits</td></tr>
<tr><td>No purchase suppression</td><td>Exit flows on order and checkout events</td><td>Post-purchase promotions feel careless</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consent imported without proof</td><td>Map timestamps and source fields</td><td>Compliance exposure during audits</td></tr>
